il 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Pr%C3%ADncipe_Moctezuma_el_Joven_llegando_al_rescate_de_los_mercaderes_sitiados_en_Ayotlan%2C_en_el_folio_6r_del_libro_IX.png/500px-Pr%C3%ADncipe_Moctezuma_el_Joven_llegando_al_rescate_de_los_mercaderes_sitiados_en_Ayotlan%2C_en_el_folio_6r_del_libro_IX.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Then-prince Moctezuma the Younger is arriving to the rescue of the merchants who were put under siege during the conquest of Ayotlan, according to the Florentine Codex. The merchants are seen talking to Moctezuma, informing him about the end of the war.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APr%C3%ADncipe_Moctezuma_el_Joven_llegando_al_rescate_de_los_mercaderes_sitiados_en_Ayotlan%2C_en_el_folio_6r_del_libro_IX.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Stone_of_the_Five_Suns.jpg/500px-Stone_of_the_Five_Suns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Stone_of_the_Five_Suns.jpg/1280px-Stone_of_the_Five_Suns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Stone_of_the_Five_Suns.jpg/500px-Stone_of_the_Five_Suns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stone of the Five Suns, a stone with inscriptions in Nahuatl writing depicting the date 15 July 1503 in the Aztec calendar. Some historians believe this to be the date on which Moctezuma was crowned.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStone_of_the_Five_Suns.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}